# Using Aries as a business owner

## Getting started
1. Sign up, then **New business**: name, goal, template, monthly agent budget, optional notes.
2. Templates and their crews:
   | Template | Top agent | Team | Suggested apps |
   |---|---|---|---|
   | Online store | Ada, CEO | Otto (Ops), June (Support), Max (Marketing), Mira (Merchandiser) | Shopify, WooCommerce, Shippo, Email, Stripe |
   | Maker / handmade | Ada, Studio Manager | Otto, June, Max | Shopify, Shippo, Email, Webhook |
   | Services business | Ada, General Manager | Sol (Sales), June (Client Success), Otto (Operations & Billing), Max | Stripe, Email, MCP, Webhook |
   | Restaurant, café or shop | Ada, General Manager | Otto (Operations & Inventory), June (Guest Relations), Max | Email, Webhook, MCP, API |
   | Software / SaaS | Ada, CEO | Linus (CTO), June (Support Lead), Max (Growth Lead) | Stripe, Email, MCP, API |
   | Creator / media | Ada, Editor-in-Chief | Sage (Researcher), Quill (Writer), Echo (Social Lead) | Stripe, Email, Webhook, MCP |
   | Start from scratch | Ada, CEO | none: Ada proposes hires | MCP, API, Webhook |
3. The CEO gets a first task automatically: write an operating plan, check connections, create the first team tasks, submit the plan for review. A **Daily brief** routine runs every 24 h.
4. Budget split: CEO gets 30% of the monthly agent budget, each team member 15%.
5. Turn on **Run the crew** (switch in the header).

## Screens (web and Android)
- **Pulse**: overview of what the crew is doing, live agents, money and orders.
- **Work**: tasks (status, priority, assignee, subtasks, comments, documents). Comment with @Name to wake an agent.
- **Store**: orders and products from connected stores; manual orders/products can be added.
- **Crew**: agents. Each has name, title, role, model, instructions, budget, heartbeat interval, pause, and **Run now**.
- **Inbox**: approvals waiting on the owner: hires, reviews, questions, budget, and real-world actions. Badge shows the count.
- **More** → Connections, Rules, Ledger (every real-world action and its result), Deliverables (documents), Plan & billing, team members, export, delete account.
- **Share to Aries**: from Android's share sheet or the PWA share target, send a customer message/text into Aries; it's routed to Support.

## Rules (the owner's control)
Each category is set to **Do it** (auto, optionally with a $ limit), **Ask me** or **Never**:
| Category | Covers | Default |
|---|---|---|
| Message customers | Emails and replies sent to customers | Ask me |
| Spend money | Shipping labels and other purchases | Ask me |
| Refunds | Money sent back to customers | Ask me |
| Change the store | Prices, product copy, fulfilling orders | Ask me |
| Payment links | Links customers can pay with | Do it, up to $500 |
| Other apps | Writes through MCP servers, APIs and webhooks | Ask me |
Recommended: start conservative, loosen once you trust the crew (e.g. auto-buy labels under $15).

## Settings
Low-stock threshold (default 3), auto-create tasks from new orders (on), monthly agent budget (default $50).

## Team members
Owners can invite members (`/members`); members can use the business but only the owner manages billing and deletion.
